  "track.animation.m.acs.st.reported": "Reported to parent",
  "track.animation.m.acs.st.target": "Animatable target",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.expand.title": "The Box is collapsed, the first measure",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.expand.explain": "On the first measure the node creates an `Animatable` EQUAL to the child's size (40 px), so there is no animation on first appearance.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.intro.expand": "The Box is collapsed, the first measure",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.after.title": "The Box is collapsed; height sits OUTSIDE animateContentSize",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.after.explain": "The chain `.height(h).animateContentSize()`: `height` is the outer modifier, and it hands the node fixed constraints of exactly h.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.intro.after": "The Box is collapsed; height sits OUTSIDE animateContentSize",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.interrupt.title": "The Box is collapsed, the first measure",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.intro.interrupt.explain": "Same as the correct version; in a moment we tap again while the Box is only partly open.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.intro.interrupt": "The Box is collapsed, the first measure",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.toggle.title": "Tap: expanded = true, the Box recomposes",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.toggle.explain": "Composition runs ONCE to build the new modifier chain with `height(160.dp)`.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.toggle": "Tap: expanded = true, the Box recomposes",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.measure.anim.title": "Measure: the child is 160, the node still reports 40",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.measure.anim.explain": "The node measures the child at 160 px, sees a new target different from `targetValue`, launches `animateTo(160)` in the node's coroutine, then reports the CURRENT value of 40 px. The 160-tall child is clipped to the 40 frame.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.measure.anim": "Measure: the child is 160, the node still reports 40",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.measure.after.title": "Measure: fixed constraints force 160 at once",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.measure.after.explain": "The node still launches the animation and returns 40, but the result is constrained to the incoming constraints (`constraints.constrain`). The constraints are fixed at 160, so the parent receives 160 at once: the Box jumps.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.measure.after": "Measure: fixed constraints force 160 at once",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.anim.title": "Frame {n}: reports {h} px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.anim.explain": "The Animatable value changes. It is state read during measurement, so only the node's measure pass re-runs (no composition); the parent places the neighbour for the new size.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.frame.anim": "Frame {n}: reports {h} px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.after.title": "Frame {n}: measures again but still reports 160 px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.after.explain": "The inner animation still runs and still re-runs the measure pass, but each time the result is forced to 160: nothing moves on screen.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.frame.after": "Frame {n}: measures again but still reports 160 px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.collapse.title": "Second tap at {h} px: expanded = false",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.collapse.explain": "The new target 40 differs from the old target 160: the node sets `startSize` = the current value ({h} px) and launches `animateTo(40)`; the new call cancels the old animation (an Animatable runs one animation at a time, chapter C6). The old animation did not finish normally, so the listener is NOT called for it.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.collapse": "Second tap at {h} px: expanded = false",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.back.title": "Frame {n}: collapsing, reports {h} px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.frame.back.explain": "It collapses from where it was, without jumping to 160 first.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.frame.back": "Frame {n}: collapsing, reports {h} px",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.expand.title": "Done: finishedListener({from} → {to})",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.expand.explain": "The animation finished normally (`AnimationEndReason.Finished`), so the listener receives the start and end sizes.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.done.expand": "Done: finishedListener({from} → {to})",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.after.title": "Done: the listener is still called, the eye saw nothing",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.after.explain": "The inner animation ran to the end, so the listener still receives ({from} → {to}); but the parent saw 160 the whole time.",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.done.after": "Done: the listener is still called, the eye saw nothing",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.interrupt.title": "Done: finishedListener({from} → {to})",
  "track.animation.m.acs.s.done.interrupt.explain": "The initial value is the size at the moment of interruption ({from} px), not 160. The KDoc says this explicitly so you can tell the DIRECTION of the change (expanding or collapsing).",
  "track.animation.m.acs.ev.done.interrupt": "Done: finishedListener({from} → {to})",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.first": "Code at the pinned commit: with no animation data yet, the node creates `Animatable(targetSize)` and returns exactly that size. [[src:an-acs-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.clip": "`animateContentSize` = `clipToBounds()` followed by the node; that is why the part of the child outside the frame is clipped while opening. [[src:an-acs-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.constrain": "Code: the result is constrained to the incoming constraints \"so that parent doesn't force center this layout\". Docs: place `animateContentSize` BEFORE `size`/`defaultMinSize`. [[src:an-acs-src]] [[src:an-composables]]",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.layoutOnly": "Bridge X1: state read during measurement only re-runs layout (Runtime chapter B7). [[src:cp-phases]]",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.interrupted": "The KDoc: if the animation is interrupted, the initial value is the size at the point of interruption, to help determine the direction of the change. [[src:an-acs-src]] [[src:book-kunneth]]",
  "track.animation.m.acs.co.wasted": "Inferred from the code (not a measurement): the invisible animation still re-runs the measure pass every frame. Fix it by reordering the modifiers.",
  "track.animation.cap.acs": "The state on the left changes the child's height; the node in the middle measures the child and reports the animating size; the parent on the right places the neighbour according to the reported size.",
  "track.animation.c5.sim.animation.acs": "Inside animateContentSize",
